WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.962
When I came down to breakfast, Uncle Silas and Aunt Sally were sitting at the table, looking sad.

2
00:00:07.963 --> 00:00:11.569
Then, we all heard noises in the yard and ran outside.

3
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:16.527
It was Tom! The doctor and some other men were carrying him on a mattress.

4
00:00:16.528 --> 00:00:20.515
Jim was there, too, with his hands tied behind his back.

5
00:00:20.516 --> 00:00:25.236
He was surrounded by the men who had chased us two nights ago.

6
00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:31.374
Aunt Sally became very busy, giving orders to servants and getting a bed ready for Tom.

7
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:35.113
Meanwhile, the men were treating Jim roughly.

8
00:00:35.114 --> 00:00:39.846
One of them even said he should be hanged because of the trouble he had caused.

9
00:00:39.847 --> 00:00:48.306
But another man said, no, the slave didn’t belong to them, and his owner would be very angry if he didn’t get his property back.

10
00:00:48.307 --> 00:00:54.141
Jim pretended that he didn’t know me. I felt terribly sad that I couldn’t help him.

11
00:00:54.142 --> 00:00:58.157
I was very relieved when the doctor told the men to treat him kindly.

12
00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:05.043
"He’s a good man," the doctor said. "He could have run away, but he stayed with me the whole time.

13
00:01:05.044 --> 00:01:10.242
He was a good nurse to that boy and helped me save his life."

14
00:01:10.243 --> 00:01:16.593
After that the men were kinder to Jim, but they still put chains on him and locked him in the shed again.

15
00:01:16.594 --> 00:01:19.939
The doctor told me that Tom was going to be fine.

16
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.268
But I knew I still had a lot to worry about.

17
00:01:23.269 --> 00:01:32.131
How would I explain why I didn’t tell the Phelpses that Sid was shot? How could I help to free Jim?

18
00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:37.266
The next day, Tom was so much better that I was allowed to go see him in his room.

19
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:41.738
He was sitting up in bed, and he began to talk to me and Aunt Sally.

20
00:01:41.739 --> 00:01:46.428
He was not very alert after his gunshot wound and his fever.

21
00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:51.831
I quickly realized he had forgotten that we were keeping many things secret.

22
00:01:51.832 --> 00:01:54.507
"How’s Jim?" he said to me.

23
00:01:54.508 --> 00:02:01.774
"He’s fine," I said quietly, frowning at him to show that he should be quiet. But he kept on talking.

24
00:02:01.775 --> 00:02:06.618
"Have you told Aunt Sally how we did everything?" continued Tom.

25
00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:11.638
"Did what ?" asked Aunt Sally, looking

26
00:02:11.639 --> 00:02:18.668
suspicious. Then, Tom told the whole story: the escape plan, the things we borrowed, the tunnel we had

27
00:02:18.669 --> 00:02:26.578
dug. Aunt Sally was astonished. When she realized how much trouble we had caused, she started to look

28
00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:34.302
angry. But Tom kept smiling. ". . . and so we helped the runaway slave get away," he

29
00:02:34.303 --> 00:02:37.771
finished. "But he didn’t get away," said Aunt

30
00:02:37.772 --> 00:02:40.580
Sally. "He’s locked in the shed right

31
00:02:40.581 --> 00:02:46.510
now." Tom’s face grew red. "No, that’s not right! You have to let him

32
00:02:46.511 --> 00:02:52.834
go. Old Mrs. Watson died two months ago, and in her will, she set Jim

33
00:02:52.835 --> 00:02:57.496
free. He’s a free man, as free as you and

34
00:02:57.497 --> 00:03:02.965
me!" Aunt Sally opened her mouth to speak, when someone else hurried into the

35
00:03:02.966 --> 00:03:10.150
room. "Why, sister!" she exclaimed. I turned to look, and there was Tom’s Aunt

36
00:03:10.151 --> 00:03:14.682
Polly! While the two sisters were hugging, I hid under the

37
00:03:14.683 --> 00:03:19.307
bed. "Come out from there, Huck Finn!" commanded Aunt

38
00:03:19.308 --> 00:03:23.223
Polly. "What mischief have you and Tom been making

39
00:03:23.224 --> 00:03:30.378
now?" Aunt Sally was very confused. "But that’s Tom under the bed, and Sid in the

40
00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:37.915
bed!" "I certainly know my own nephew Tom—I’ve looked after him since he was a baby," said Aunt

41
00:03:37.916 --> 00:03:46.807
Polly. "And I know Huckleberry, too! When I got that letter from you saying Sid was visiting, I had to come and see what was

42
00:03:46.808 --> 00:03:51.675
wrong. Sid is safe at home, where he should

43
00:03:51.676 --> 00:03:58.539
be." The first chance I got to talk to Tom by himself, I asked him why he never told us that Jim was a free

44
00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:04.485
man. "I wanted to have adventures," Tom said. "I wanted to free him from

45
00:04:04.486 --> 00:04:09.284
prison. Then, I wanted to go down the Mississippi on the raft with you and

46
00:04:09.285 --> 00:04:14.638
him. I planned to wait until we got to New Orleans and then tell Jim the

47
00:04:14.639 --> 00:04:20.394
truth." Aunt Sally and Uncle Silas freed Jim from the shed as soon as they heard Tom’s

48
00:04:20.395 --> 00:04:24.343
story. They fed him a good meal and gave him some clean

49
00:04:24.344 --> 00:04:28.718
clothes. Then Tom gave Jim forty dollars to start his new

50
00:04:28.719 --> 00:04:32.344
life. "Remember what I told you, Huck?" Jim said to

51
00:04:32.345 --> 00:04:39.779
me. "If a man has hair on his chest like me, it means he is going to be rich some day. And now I

52
00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:44.242
am!" Once Tom was feeling better, he wanted Jim to stay for a few

53
00:04:44.243 --> 00:04:49.272
days. "We could dress up and pretend to be pirates," Tom

54
00:04:49.273 --> 00:04:51.926
suggested. "I don't have any money for pirate

55
00:04:51.927 --> 00:04:56.845
clothes. I guess by now Pap got all our money from Judge Thatcher," I

56
00:04:56.846 --> 00:05:02.554
said. "No, he hasn’t," said Tom. "We still have our six thousand

57
00:05:02.555 --> 00:05:07.443
dollars. Pap hasn’t come back—at least, he hadn’t when I left

58
00:05:07.444 --> 00:05:15.459
home." Then, Jim said in a serious voice, "Your Pap isn’t ever coming back, Huck. You don’t have to worry about

59
00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:22.780
that." At first, he didn’t want to explain how he knew this, but I wouldn’t stop asking

60
00:05:22.781 --> 00:05:28.346
questions. Finally Jim said, "Do you remember that house that we found, floating down the

61
00:05:28.347 --> 00:05:29.943
river?" I

62
00:05:29.944 --> 00:05:35.071
nodded. "Do you remember that there was a body inside, and I told you not to

63
00:05:35.072 --> 00:05:40.961
look? Well, I recognized his face—it was your

64
00:05:40.962 --> 00:05:44.886
Pap." Well, now I’ve finished everything I wanted to

65
00:05:44.887 --> 00:05:49.316
write. Tom’s leg has healed. And he kept the bullet for a

66
00:05:49.317 --> 00:05:54.818
souvenir. Aunt Sally wants to adopt me and civilize me. But I might run

67
00:05:54.819 --> 00:06:00.132
